        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Royal Centre tram stop, Nottingham Trent University tram stop, Victoria Centre, Cornerhouse, Nottingham, England\n- Organizations: Nottingham Trent University, Yorkshire Carnegie\n- Buildings: Newton Building, Arkwright Building\n- Topics: City Campus, rugby union\n\nFacts:\n- Victoria Centre is a shopping centre in Nottingham, England, that was constructed between 1967 and 1972.\n- Thomas P. Ryder was born on 21 February 1985 in Nottingham, England.\n- Thomas P. Ryder was a rugby union player who played at lock and latterly played for Yorkshire Carnegie in the RFU Championship.\n- Royal Centre tram stop is close to the Cornerhouse, the Victoria Centre, and the Newton Building of Nottingham Trent University.\n- Much of Nottingham Trent University's City Campus is closer to Nottingham Trent University tram stop than to Royal Centre tram stop.\n- Nottingham Trent University tram stop is near the university's flagship Arkwright Building and Newton Building to the south.\n- The Newton Building is closer to Royal Centre tram stop than to Nottingham Trent University tram stop.",
